# ASTERIX Category 062, System Track Data: one data block holding one record.
# Public. Written from EUROCONTROL-SPEC-0149-9 Edition 1.21; the items mapped
# are the ones the CAT062 encoder of USAREUR-AF/open-billie writes. I/O is hex
# text. Needs engine version 0.8 (`layout sequential`). See pack.md.
#
#   octet 1       CAT = 62
#   octets 2-3    LEN, the length of the data block in octets, CAT and LEN included
#   FSPEC         octets of 7 presence bits and an extension bit; bit n is FRN n
#   then          the items whose FSPEC bit is 1, in FRN order
#
# An FRN this pack does not map has no `if` block: a record with that FSPEC
# bit set fails with `malformed-wire` (ruling 1 of engine-spec 0.8), and
# encode never sets the bit.
#
# I062/130 is the height above the WGS-84 ellipsoid in steps of 6.25 ft.
# 6.25 ft is 1.905 m exactly, written here as the fraction 381/200, so `hae`
# is in metres.
#
# I062/080: each mapped bit has its raw key in `cat062`; CNF, SIM, TSE and CST
# also bind the `track` flag of the same meaning with an `also` line. CNF is 0
# for a confirmed track, the reverse of `track.confirmed`; the table `cnf`
# turns it over. Encode writes the raw key when the entity has it, else the
# flag, else the default. The defaults are on the flags: MON 1, SIM, TSE and
# CST 0, so the item always has its first part and three extents. The other
# status bits are `pad`: dropped on decode, written 0.
format     asterix-cat062
version    0.3.0
distribution public
source  "EUROCONTROL-SPEC-0149-9, Specification for Surveillance Data Exchange ASTERIX Part 9 Category 062, SDPS Track Messages, Edition 1.21, 5 June 2025, https://www.eurocontrol.int/sites/default/files/2025-06/asterix-cat062-system-track-data-p9-ed1-21.pdf"
source  "USAREUR-AF/open-billie runtime/rust/translator/src/cat062.rs (Apache-2.0): which items its encoder writes, and the blocks it produces, used as vectors"
uses       track
uses       cat062
wire       bits
layout     sequential
bit_order  msb
map     cnf  0  1
map     cnf  1  0
kind    track
when    8  62                                # CAT
# the four items the specification requires in every record. SAC and SIC come
# from the caller; the time of day and the track number follow from `time_ms`
# and `uid` (model/cat062.def); CNF has no default, so the flag is required.
requires cat062.sac cat062.sic cat062.time_of_day_s cat062.track_number track.confirmed
default cat062.mon          1
default cat062.mrh          0
default cat062.src          0
default track.simulated     0
default track.final_update  0
default track.coasting      0
length  16 whole                             # LEN
presence fspec fx
if fspec.1                                   # FRN 1, I062/010 Data Source Identifier
  field  cat062.sac  8  uint
  field  cat062.sic  8  uint
end
if fspec.3                                   # FRN 3, I062/015 Service Identification
  field  cat062.service_id  8  uint
end
if fspec.4                                   # FRN 4, I062/070 Time Of Track Information, 1/128 s
  field  cat062.time_of_day_s  24  uscale:1/128
end
if fspec.5                                   # FRN 5, I062/105 Calculated Position in WGS-84, 180/2^25 degrees
  field  lat  32  sscale:180/33554432
  field  lon  32  sscale:180/33554432
end
if fspec.7                                   # FRN 7, I062/185 Calculated Track Velocity (Cartesian), 0.25 m/s
  field  track.vel_east_ms   16  sscale:1/4    # Vx
  field  track.vel_north_ms  16  sscale:1/4    # Vy: the y-axis points to geographical north
end
if fspec.12                                  # FRN 12, I062/040 Track Number
  field  cat062.track_number  16  uint
end
if fspec.13                                  # FRN 13, I062/080 Track Status
  chain
    field  cat062.mon  1  uint                  # MON
    pad    1                                    # SPI
    field  cat062.mrh  1  uint                  # MRH: 1 = geometric height more reliable
    field  cat062.src  3  uint                  # SRC: source of the I062/130 altitude, 0 none, 1 GNSS
    field  cat062.cnf  1  uint                  # CNF: 0 = confirmed, 1 = tentative
    also   track.confirmed  via cnf
    fx
    field  cat062.sim  1  uint                  # SIM
    also   track.simulated
    field  cat062.tse  1  uint                  # TSE: last message for the track
    also   track.final_update
    pad    5                                    # TSB, FPC, AFF, STP, KOS
    fx
    pad    7                                    # second extent: AMA, MD4, ME, MI, MD5
    fx
    field  cat062.cst  1  uint                  # CST
    also   track.coasting
    pad    6                                    # PSR, SSR, MDS, ADS, SUC, AAC
    fx
    pad    7                                    # fourth extent: SDS, EMS, PFT, FPLT
    fx
    pad    7                                    # fifth extent: DUPT, DUPF, DUPM, SFC, IDD, IEC, MLAT
    fx
    pad    7                                    # sixth extent: M5I and spare bits
    fx
  end
end
if fspec.18                                  # FRN 18, I062/130 Calculated Track Geometric Altitude, 6.25 ft
  field  hae  16  sscale:381/200
end
if fspec.34                                  # FRN 34, I062/RE Reserved Expansion Field
  length 8 bytes plus 1                      # the length octet counts itself; the content is not mapped
  end
end
if fspec.35                                  # FRN 35, I062/SP Special Purpose Field
  length 8 bytes plus 1                      # the length octet counts itself; the content is not mapped
  end
end
